        <name>setActive</name>
        <qualifiedname>sf::RenderTexture::setActive</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classsf_1_1RenderTarget_1adc225ead22a70843ffa9b7eebefa0ce1">setActive</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>active</declname>
          <defval>true</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Activate or deactivate the render-texture for rendering. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function makes the render-texture&apos;s context current for future OpenGL rendering operations (so you shouldn&apos;t care about it if you&apos;re not doing direct OpenGL stuff). Only one context can be current in a thread, so if you want to draw OpenGL geometry to another render target (like a <ref refid="classsf_1_1RenderWindow" kindref="compound">RenderWindow</ref>) don&apos;t forget to activate it again.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>active</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> to activate, <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> to deactivate</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if operation was successful, <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> otherwise </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
